1
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:12,367
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:38,967 --> 00:00:40,567
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:41,933 --> 00:00:42,833
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:45,267 --> 00:00:46,733
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

5
00:00:55,533 --> 00:00:56,833
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:57,800 --> 00:00:59,433
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:00,900
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,233
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:01:02,367 --> 00:01:03,933
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:05,967 --> 00:01:07,300
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

11
00:01:10,067 --> 00:01:11,667
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

12
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:17,433
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

13
00:01:17,533 --> 00:01:19,333
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

14
00:01:20,367 --> 00:01:21,767
[GLASS SHATTERING]

15
00:01:21,867 --> 00:01:24,800
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

16
00:01:25,467 --> 00:01:28,467
[ENGINES REVVING]

17
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:31,500
[TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:32,367 --> 00:01:35,100
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:35,233 --> 00:01:36,267
[GUNSHOTS]

20
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:37,633
[TIRES SCREECHING]

21
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:39,133
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

22
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:40,867
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:45,367 --> 00:01:46,733
<i> Where is what you promised me?</i>

24
00:01:46,867 --> 00:01:50,467
<i>You said you'd find a way
to get your father surgery.</i>

25
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:51,967
<i> Where is it?! Where is it?!</i>

26
00:01:52,067 --> 00:01:53,133
<i> I found work, Auntie.</i>

27
00:01:53,267 --> 00:01:55,967
<i>I just need to locate someone,
then I'll get paid.</i>

28
00:01:56,100 --> 00:02:02,867
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

29
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:08,800
[MOTOR ENGINE REVVING]

30
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:09,900
[TIRES SCREECH]

31
00:02:10,033 --> 00:02:12,133
[MOTOR ENGINE ROARS]

32
00:02:12,233 --> 00:02:14,700
<i>Are they really
going to help us?</i>

33
00:02:14,867 --> 00:02:18,500
<i> Provide a lawyer
</i>if we decide to sue the police?

34
00:02:18,633 --> 00:02:23,200
<i>But if we sue the cops...
it's like picking up a rock</i>

35
00:02:23,367 --> 00:02:25,833
<i>and smashing it
against our own heads.</i>

36
00:02:25,967 --> 00:02:27,433
<i>The patient's condition
is critical.</i>

37
00:02:27,567 --> 00:02:29,000
<i> He needs surgery right away.</i>

38
00:02:29,133 --> 00:02:30,267
<i> I'll find a way right now</i>

39
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:32,033
<i>to get my father
into surgery immediately.</i>

40
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:34,167
<i> Pa, please hold on tight.</i>

41
00:02:34,267 --> 00:02:37,200
<i>I'm doing everything I can
so you'll get better soon.</i>

42
00:02:37,367 --> 00:02:38,700
<i> I promise...</i>

43
00:02:38,867 --> 00:02:40,833
<i>I won't let anything
happen to you, Pa.</i>

44
00:02:40,967 --> 00:02:42,867
<i>Even if I have to risk
my very own life...</i>

45
00:02:43,033 --> 00:02:46,100
<i>I won't let anything bad
befall you, Pa.</i>

46
00:02:46,233 --> 00:02:50,267
[DOOR OPENS, CLOSES]

47
00:02:50,433 --> 00:02:53,733
Stop pressuring Sam like that.

48
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:55,400
It's not helping her at all.

49
00:02:55,567 --> 00:02:57,867
Sir, I'm not pressuring her,

50
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:01,533
she's just easily scared.
Maybe she's insecure?

51
00:03:01,667 --> 00:03:04,700
I just want her to do better...

52
00:03:04,833 --> 00:03:08,300
even if I don't trust her.

53
00:03:08,433 --> 00:03:12,033
You question every
single thing Sam does.

54
00:03:12,133 --> 00:03:14,367
She's actually very skilled.

55
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:15,733
Skilled?

56
00:03:17,133 --> 00:03:20,033
Depends who you ask.

57
00:03:20,133 --> 00:03:23,533
Excuse me, sir.
I have things to take care of.

58
00:03:23,667 --> 00:03:27,400
[BROODING MUSIC PLAYING]

59
00:03:27,533 --> 00:03:30,733
[DOOR OPENS, CLOSES]

60
00:03:33,933 --> 00:03:36,167
Mr. Chan...
(In Cantonese) Happy New Year!

61
00:03:36,300 --> 00:03:37,767
[MR. CHAN] Victor!

62
00:03:37,933 --> 00:03:40,767
(In Cantonese)<i> Wishing you
</i> a prosperous New Year!

63
00:03:40,933 --> 00:03:44,600
Mr. Chan, I'll see you later.
I have your gold.

64
00:03:44,767 --> 00:03:46,233
See?

65
00:03:46,333 --> 00:03:47,933
[MR. CHAN]
<i> Good! Good!</i>

66
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:51,567
<i>Okay, Victor, I'll see you
later. Give me a call, okay?</i>

67
00:03:51,700 --> 00:03:53,133
Okay, I'll see you later.

68
00:03:53,267 --> 00:03:54,633
[DOOR OPENS]

69
00:03:56,567 --> 00:04:01,167
So Victor, are you meeting
with Mr. Chan now?

70
00:04:01,300 --> 00:04:02,967
Yes, Pa.

71
00:04:03,133 --> 00:04:04,700
We're meeting later.

72
00:04:04,833 --> 00:04:07,367
But first,
I'm heading to Lao's wedding.

73
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:10,267
You'd put that ahead
of our business?

74
00:04:11,667 --> 00:04:13,833
Lao's one of my people, Ma.

75
00:04:13,967 --> 00:04:17,600
You have several deals
to finalize today.

76
00:04:17,733 --> 00:04:19,867
That should be
your top priority.

77
00:04:22,467 --> 00:04:25,500
Darling, let Victor be.

78
00:04:25,633 --> 00:04:27,200
He knows what he's doing.

79
00:04:27,367 --> 00:04:28,800
When we were just starting out,

80
00:04:28,900 --> 00:04:32,800
we never wasted time
on trivial things like that.

81
00:04:32,933 --> 00:04:36,000
That's what
you should inherit, Victor.

82
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:40,800
Mariano and I worked so hard
to build all of this.

83
00:04:40,900 --> 00:04:44,633
So I want you
to prioritize the business.

84
00:04:44,767 --> 00:04:47,067
This is for our family.

85
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:49,567
Yes, Ma.

86
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:51,900
Everything's all set
for tonight.

87
00:04:53,033 --> 00:04:54,867
I've handled worse than this,
Ma.

88
00:04:58,600 --> 00:04:59,967
Let's go.

89
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:06,000
[BRIEFCASES SNAPPING SHUT]

90
00:05:06,100 --> 00:05:12,400
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

91
00:05:12,533 --> 00:05:13,500
[VICTOR] Lee.

92
00:05:13,633 --> 00:05:14,700
Yes, boss?

93
00:05:14,867 --> 00:05:16,767
Go to the Jade Imperial now.

94
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:19,500
If Mr. Chan gets there first,
take care of him, alright?

95
00:05:19,633 --> 00:05:21,000
Sure, boss.

96
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:24,667
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

97
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:26,600
How was the thing
I asked you for?

98
00:05:26,733 --> 00:05:28,400
Our flight to Malaysia
will be at midnight.

99
00:05:28,533 --> 00:05:30,267
Everything's ready.

100
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:31,500
And me?

101
00:05:31,633 --> 00:05:33,067
Where do you want me to go?

102
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:35,167
Attend the wedding with me.

103
00:05:36,133 --> 00:05:38,100
Just stick close to me
the whole evening, got it?

104
00:05:42,067 --> 00:05:49,033
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [INTENSE ROCK MUSIC PLAYING]

105
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:57,367
[TIRES SCREECHING]

106
00:06:01,833 --> 00:06:08,900
[FESTIVAL INSTRUMENTS PLAYING]

107
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:19,067
[PEOPLE CLAMORING]

108
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:23,800
[ENGINES REVVING]

109
00:06:23,933 --> 00:06:31,000
[INTENSE ROCK MUSIC CONTINUES]

110
00:06:31,933 --> 00:06:34,067
[FESTIVAL INSTRUMENTS
PLAYING CONTINUES]

111
00:06:34,167 --> 00:06:38,500
[ENGINES REVVING]

112
00:06:38,633 --> 00:06:39,833
[TIRES SCREECH]

113
00:06:42,633 --> 00:06:43,800
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

114
00:06:48,500 --> 00:06:49,633
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

115
00:06:56,133 --> 00:07:01,300
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVVING]

116
00:07:01,467 --> 00:07:02,600
[TIRES SCREECH]

117
00:07:02,700 --> 00:07:09,767
[INTENSE ROCK MUSIC CONTINUES]

118
00:07:11,633 --> 00:07:18,767
[ENGINE REVVING]

119
00:07:25,500 --> 00:07:27,033
[METAL CLANGING]

120
00:07:27,167 --> 00:07:33,967
[FESTIVAL INSTRUMENTS
PLAYING CONTINUES]

121
00:07:34,100 --> 00:07:38,700
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVVING]

122
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:40,633
- [WHISTLE BLOWS]
- You can't be here!

123
00:07:40,733 --> 00:07:42,533
- [ENGINE ROARS]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

124
00:07:42,667 --> 00:07:49,633
[ENGINE REVVING]

125
00:07:49,767 --> 00:07:56,767
[INTENSE ROCK MUSIC CONTINUES]

126
00:08:00,033 --> 00:08:07,000
[FESTIVAL INSTRUMENT
PLAYING CONTINUES]

127
00:08:19,100 --> 00:08:24,200
[PEOPLE CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

128
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:27,033
[BINOY] Even his height?
Is he tall? Short? What?

129
00:08:27,167 --> 00:08:28,900
[TOLITS] I have no idea
what to do, man.

130
00:08:29,067 --> 00:08:31,100
Gabo is asking
for the impossible here!

131
00:08:31,233 --> 00:08:33,767
We're looking for someone
we haven't even met!

132
00:08:33,900 --> 00:08:35,367
It's much easier to rob
and kidnap someone

133
00:08:35,500 --> 00:08:37,367
than to look for someone
you haven't even met!

134
00:08:37,467 --> 00:08:38,700
Hold it!

135
00:08:38,833 --> 00:08:40,700
I thought you wanted
to turn over a new leaf?

136
00:08:40,833 --> 00:08:43,067
And weren't you the ones
who insisted to join us?

137
00:08:43,233 --> 00:08:46,300
We do want to turn over
a new leaf, Tekla.

138
00:08:46,433 --> 00:08:47,967
Plus, if we don't join Gabo,

139
00:08:48,100 --> 00:08:49,933
Mr. Paquito will be
on our case for sure!

140
00:08:50,067 --> 00:08:51,900
He believes that we're
stabbing Gabo in the back!

141
00:08:52,067 --> 00:08:54,933
Oh? What's the matter then?
Why are you all making a fuss?

142
00:08:55,100 --> 00:08:56,833
We didn't force you
to come with us

143
00:08:56,967 --> 00:08:58,433
but you keep on tagging along.

144
00:08:58,600 --> 00:08:59,567
Alright, alright!

145
00:08:59,667 --> 00:09:01,067
We'll join you guys.

146
00:09:01,200 --> 00:09:04,800
We'll follow anything you say
even if it's to look for an ant!

147
00:09:04,933 --> 00:09:07,000
Just let us join your group.

148
00:09:07,133 --> 00:09:09,600
If you really want to become
a part of our group,

149
00:09:09,767 --> 00:09:10,933
don't be picky!

150
00:09:11,100 --> 00:09:13,067
Always heed Gabo's orders!

151
00:09:13,167 --> 00:09:15,933
Exactly. And please,
can't you three just be grateful

152
00:09:16,100 --> 00:09:17,733
that we gave you a job, huh?

153
00:09:17,833 --> 00:09:19,400
It's supposed to be
just the four of us.

154
00:09:19,533 --> 00:09:21,967
Now we have to split the money
with you too.

155
00:09:23,433 --> 00:09:24,933
Let's move.

156
00:09:25,100 --> 00:09:26,567
- Move!
- Let's go.

157
00:09:27,567 --> 00:09:28,767
[IPE] Get a move on!

158
00:09:28,900 --> 00:09:30,100
[BINOY] We're coming!

159
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:32,300
[BEEPS]

160
00:09:32,467 --> 00:09:35,667
Alpha 1, onsite.
What's your status?

161
00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:37,100
Alpha 2, in position.

162
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:38,700
Negative visuals on the target.

163
00:09:38,833 --> 00:09:40,300
Status of the others?

164
00:09:40,467 --> 00:09:42,433
[SEBASTIAN]<i> All possible
</i> locations covered.

165
00:09:42,567 --> 00:09:44,033
<i> Tiger isn't here yet.</i>

166
00:09:44,167 --> 00:09:45,267
Copy.

167
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:46,600
Maintain surveillance.

168
00:09:46,733 --> 00:09:48,167
Copy that.

169
00:09:48,300 --> 00:09:54,867
- [STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]
- [FESTIVAL INSTRUMENTS PLAYING]

170
00:09:56,533 --> 00:10:02,000
[ENGINE REVVING]

171
00:10:08,867 --> 00:10:10,367
[FLAMES CRACKLING]

172
00:10:10,500 --> 00:10:17,300
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

173
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:36,767
[UMALI] Deploy more police
in Chinatown.

174
00:10:36,900 --> 00:10:39,700
We need to
maintain order there.

175
00:10:39,800 --> 00:10:41,833
Especially today,
since it's Chinese New Year.

176
00:10:41,967 --> 00:10:44,067
- Do you understand?
- [MEDINA] Yes, sir

177
00:10:45,033 --> 00:10:47,267
[ESTRELLA] These are the reports
from the other night.

178
00:10:47,433 --> 00:10:49,600
[MAX] You should run
those fingerprints already.

179
00:10:49,767 --> 00:10:51,733
The Chief has been looking
for that for so long.

180
00:10:53,567 --> 00:10:54,900
Yes, sir?

181
00:10:57,400 --> 00:10:58,733
I got you something.

182
00:10:58,867 --> 00:11:00,433
We went around
Chinatown earlier,

183
00:11:00,567 --> 00:11:02,367
- and I thought of you.
- Here.

184
00:11:02,467 --> 00:11:04,100
- Hmm.
- Moon cake.

185
00:11:04,267 --> 00:11:05,667
I hope you like it.

186
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:13,700
Oh, sir, I'm sorry.

187
00:11:13,833 --> 00:11:15,233
I'm actually allergic to them.

188
00:11:15,333 --> 00:11:16,133
On moon cakes?!

189
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:17,767
No, they're actually
my favorite!

190
00:11:17,900 --> 00:11:19,967
I'm actually allergic
to corny jokes.

191
00:11:20,100 --> 00:11:21,367
Hmm.

192
00:11:21,500 --> 00:11:23,033
Alright, sir.

193
00:11:23,167 --> 00:11:24,267
Wait a minute.

194
00:11:26,167 --> 00:11:28,300
I'm just trying
to be kind, Jacinto.

195
00:11:29,333 --> 00:11:31,367
How is General Jacinto
doing, by the way?

196
00:11:32,333 --> 00:11:33,700
My dad?!

197
00:11:33,833 --> 00:11:35,467
He's alright, sir.

198
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:37,633
He's disappointed in you.

199
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:40,467
Because you failed
to do the demolition.

200
00:11:41,467 --> 00:11:45,967
That's why I think we should
focus on our job, sir.

201
00:11:48,433 --> 00:11:49,567
Goodbye, sir.

202
00:11:49,700 --> 00:11:51,133
Wait.

203
00:11:51,267 --> 00:11:53,333
Take this, please.

204
00:11:53,500 --> 00:11:55,800
[PLASTIC RUSTLING]

205
00:11:55,933 --> 00:11:57,500
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

206
00:12:00,333 --> 00:12:01,333
[MAX] Enjoy.

207
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:05,400
Thank you, sir.
These are my favorite.

208
00:12:05,533 --> 00:12:06,800
Thank you!

209
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:10,233
Your favorite?

210
00:12:10,367 --> 00:12:11,833
That's my favorite too.

211
00:12:13,333 --> 00:12:15,233
[CHUCKLING SOFTLY]

212
00:12:16,400 --> 00:12:17,467
Sir.

213
00:12:20,067 --> 00:12:22,300
You've been trying
to win her over for so long,

214
00:12:23,367 --> 00:12:25,133
but you're always
getting rejected.

215
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:28,200
Why on earth

216
00:12:28,367 --> 00:12:30,467
did you choose to pursue
the General's daughter?

217
00:12:30,567 --> 00:12:31,700
You know what,

218
00:12:31,833 --> 00:12:33,167
Santos,

219
00:12:34,467 --> 00:12:35,533
she isn't just beautiful.

220
00:12:35,700 --> 00:12:37,700
Max is also wealthy
and intelligent.

221
00:12:37,867 --> 00:12:39,367
And her father
is also the General.

222
00:12:40,833 --> 00:12:42,433
If I manage to win her over,

223
00:12:43,300 --> 00:12:44,967
my reputation across the entire
police force will improve.

224
00:12:45,067 --> 00:12:46,667
- Do you understand?
- [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

225
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:48,500
So don't worry, Santos.

226
00:12:48,667 --> 00:12:50,500
I'll win her over eventually.

227
00:12:52,767 --> 00:12:53,967
[DOOR CLICKS]

228
00:12:54,933 --> 00:12:56,200
[DOOR CLOSES, CLICKS]

229
00:12:57,700 --> 00:12:59,733
- [DOOR CLOSES]
- Ma'am.

230
00:12:59,900 --> 00:13:02,367
Umali certainly has
a lot of nerve, doesn't he?

231
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:03,633
When will he give up?

232
00:13:03,767 --> 00:13:05,900
I don't know, he's disgusting.
He thinks he's so handsome.

233
00:13:06,067 --> 00:13:07,733
Does he think he can win me over

234
00:13:07,867 --> 00:13:09,467
just because he's the Captain?
No way!

235
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:10,633
But, ma'am...

236
00:13:10,767 --> 00:13:13,067
Your father's reputation
scares people.

237
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:16,400
He was silent once
you mentioned the General.

238
00:13:16,567 --> 00:13:20,700
If you only knew. He's also
incredibly strict with us

239
00:13:20,833 --> 00:13:22,067
It's like we're still
in the academy.

240
00:13:22,233 --> 00:13:23,433
There's nothing we can do.

241
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:25,233
His word is always final.

242
00:13:25,367 --> 00:13:29,767
I suppose you dream of becoming
a general, too, ma'am?

243
00:13:29,933 --> 00:13:31,667
- Me?
- Mm-hmm.

244
00:13:31,800 --> 00:13:33,600
No.

245
00:13:33,733 --> 00:13:36,867
That's his dream
for his only son.

246
00:13:36,967 --> 00:13:40,400
Oh!
So, you have a brother, ma'am?

247
00:13:40,533 --> 00:13:42,100
Is he also a police?

248
00:13:43,900 --> 00:13:45,900
Estrella,
that ballistic report...

249
00:13:46,967 --> 00:13:49,400
[SIGHS] I might forget about it.

250
00:13:49,533 --> 00:13:50,600
- Oh, alright.
- Yes.

251
00:13:50,767 --> 00:13:51,867
Thank you for this, ma'am.

252
00:13:51,967 --> 00:13:53,433
- [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]
- Hope you'll like it.

253
00:13:53,567 --> 00:13:54,700
[CHUCKLES]

254
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:59,500
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

255
00:13:59,667 --> 00:14:02,300
[DOOR CREAKS OPEN, CLOSES]

256
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:08,133
Later,
it's Chinese New Year time.

257
00:14:09,133 --> 00:14:10,967
There's going to be
a lot of people.

258
00:14:11,800 --> 00:14:13,100
That's why...

259
00:14:13,900 --> 00:14:15,533
I want to earn
a lot of money.

260
00:14:15,667 --> 00:14:18,600
- Do you understand?
- [MAN] You can count on us.

261
00:14:18,733 --> 00:14:22,133
Don't ever come back here
unless you have the money.

262
00:14:22,267 --> 00:14:23,967
- Yes, boss.
- Alright. Go!

263
00:14:24,133 --> 00:14:25,433
[MAN] Let's go.

264
00:14:25,567 --> 00:14:32,400
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

265
00:14:33,467 --> 00:14:35,467
- [MAN] Everyone, watch.
- How is it here?

266
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:38,167
[VON] Django. The news is out
that Gabo has taken in

267
00:14:38,300 --> 00:14:40,800
Binoy, Tolits, and Daboy.
They're now part of his group!

268
00:14:40,933 --> 00:14:42,300
What?

269
00:14:44,433 --> 00:14:46,167
Those idiots!

270
00:14:47,700 --> 00:14:49,500
They just heard that

271
00:14:49,667 --> 00:14:52,500
I got outsmarted by Gabo,
and they betrayed me!

272
00:14:52,667 --> 00:14:55,000
Gabo is building up his forces.

273
00:14:56,033 --> 00:14:57,900
He's recruiting people
to go up against me.

274
00:14:58,033 --> 00:14:59,233
[ROMY] It won't be long before

275
00:14:59,367 --> 00:15:00,933
they start acting
like they own the place.

276
00:15:01,033 --> 00:15:02,333
That's not going to happen.

277
00:15:03,067 --> 00:15:05,300
I've known for a long time

278
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:07,533
that Gabo wants
to rule over Ginintuang Lupa.

279
00:15:07,700 --> 00:15:08,967
But I won't let that happen.

280
00:15:09,067 --> 00:15:10,867
As long as I'm alive,

281
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:12,433
this is our place!

282
00:15:13,567 --> 00:15:14,633
[PAQUITO] Django.

283
00:15:14,733 --> 00:15:17,367
Before Gabo gets the chance
to gain more influence,

284
00:15:18,300 --> 00:15:20,200
you should cut his horns
while it's early.

285
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:23,200
We're going to build up
our forces, Pa.

286
00:15:24,067 --> 00:15:25,600
I'll make sure...

287
00:15:26,533 --> 00:15:28,867
that Gabo won't be able
to make a move.

288
00:15:29,033 --> 00:15:30,700
Continue training!

289
00:15:30,867 --> 00:15:32,767
- You three are next!
- [MAN] Go ahead.

290
00:15:32,900 --> 00:15:34,100
Let's go.

291
00:15:34,233 --> 00:15:39,467
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

292
00:15:40,267 --> 00:15:47,233
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

293
00:15:48,267 --> 00:15:51,900
[GONG CLANGING]

294
00:15:51,900 --> 00:15:58,867
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

295
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:05,000
[VAN DOOR SLIDING OPEN]

296
00:16:11,933 --> 00:16:14,600
We'll scout the area.
Sharpen your eyes.

297
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:19,233
We need to see Mr. Chan.
He'll bring us to Tiger.

298
00:16:19,233 --> 00:16:21,233
[KAREN] Are you sure
Mr. Chan is there?

299
00:16:21,233 --> 00:16:22,233
Can't we move closer

300
00:16:22,233 --> 00:16:24,267
so we can get a better look
at the place?

301
00:16:24,267 --> 00:16:26,433
Alright, listen.
Bullet! Borromeo.

302
00:16:27,200 --> 00:16:28,600
Look around inside.

303
00:16:28,600 --> 00:16:30,900
Find out if Mr. Chan
is there, okay?

304
00:16:30,900 --> 00:16:33,333
- Yes, sir.
- Let's go.

305
00:16:36,433 --> 00:16:42,867
[GONG CLANGING]

306
00:16:42,900 --> 00:16:45,600
How will we know if the person
we're looking for is here?

307
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:47,467
- Oh, I don't know.
- Well, that's easy!

308
00:16:47,467 --> 00:16:50,333
Let's rob this place,
and ask where Mr. Chan is.

309
00:16:50,333 --> 00:16:52,500
- Ow! Ouch! You jerk!
- What's with you?

310
00:16:52,500 --> 00:16:54,333
- Rob it on your own.
- That's not our job.

311
00:16:54,333 --> 00:16:57,167
Our job is to find out
who owns that.

312
00:16:57,167 --> 00:17:00,467
Shh! What's with you?
Shut up, you're too noisy!

313
00:17:00,467 --> 00:17:04,267
Someone might overhear that
we're looking for Mr. Chan.

314
00:17:05,167 --> 00:17:08,300
It'd be better to wait for Gabo.

315
00:17:08,300 --> 00:17:09,433
How are we going
to wait for Gabo

316
00:17:09,433 --> 00:17:10,967
when his father's
in the hospital?

317
00:17:10,967 --> 00:17:13,167
We might miss the man
he's looking for.

318
00:17:13,167 --> 00:17:15,467
We were given
a picture, remember?

319
00:17:16,967 --> 00:17:19,967
You're still complaining?
Are you still coming with us?

320
00:17:19,967 --> 00:17:22,700
Yeah, we're joining you!
We'll do whatever you want.

321
00:17:22,700 --> 00:17:23,900
What do you want to do?

322
00:17:24,467 --> 00:17:26,533
Want to eat first?
Let's eat first.

323
00:17:26,533 --> 00:17:29,700
- We have a job to do, remember?
- Alright, we're not eating.

324
00:17:29,700 --> 00:17:33,467
[GONG CLANGING]

325
00:17:33,467 --> 00:17:40,400
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

326
00:17:48,700 --> 00:17:49,967
Uh, miss?

327
00:17:50,567 --> 00:17:51,500
Hello!

328
00:17:51,500 --> 00:17:54,300
Miss, how much
do these cost nowadays?

329
00:17:54,300 --> 00:17:57,167
[STAFF] The 18-carat necklace
is around 8000 pesos.

330
00:17:57,167 --> 00:17:58,500
That's a bit high.
Could you...

331
00:17:59,467 --> 00:18:01,033
...maybe cheapen it?

332
00:18:01,033 --> 00:18:04,733
If we buy a lot,
could you give us a discount?

333
00:18:04,733 --> 00:18:07,100
Only my boss can decide on that.

334
00:18:07,700 --> 00:18:10,200
- Is your boss here?
- Yes, he is.

335
00:18:10,200 --> 00:18:15,333
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

336
00:18:15,333 --> 00:18:18,633
What if we split
into two groups?

337
00:18:18,633 --> 00:18:20,400
So we don't look sketchy.

338
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:22,200
The three of you can go
somewhere far,

339
00:18:22,233 --> 00:18:23,600
so I won't be able to smell you.

340
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:25,500
Then let's come up
with our own gimmick,

341
00:18:25,500 --> 00:18:27,733
so we don't look stupid
waiting here.

342
00:18:28,500 --> 00:18:29,600
No, let's do it this way.

343
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:32,200
Let's split into two groups
to avoid suspicion.

344
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:33,433
Let's stay on the other side.

345
00:18:33,433 --> 00:18:34,733
[TEKLA] You just repeated
what I said!

346
00:18:34,733 --> 00:18:36,767
- This jerk...
- You're such a jerk.

347
00:18:36,767 --> 00:18:38,433
- You just changed her tone.
- Go!

348
00:18:38,433 --> 00:18:41,400
- Come on, come on!
- Survey properly!

349
00:18:47,267 --> 00:18:48,633
Alright, miss, how about...

350
00:18:49,433 --> 00:18:52,400
We'll look around,
and just come back

351
00:18:52,400 --> 00:18:56,100
- if we don't see anything else.
- Okay, I'll wait here.

352
00:18:56,133 --> 00:18:57,500
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

353
00:19:02,233 --> 00:19:04,267
[BINOY] Where will we look
for them when we're separated?

354
00:19:04,267 --> 00:19:07,233
Let it go and just follow.
Tekla's already mad.

355
00:19:07,233 --> 00:19:09,600
You know she stabs people
when she's mad.

356
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:12,433
- Ow! Ow, ouch!
- Hey! Hey.

357
00:19:12,433 --> 00:19:14,267
- Are you blind?!
- Me, blind?

358
00:19:15,067 --> 00:19:16,567
You didn't see me
when I'm this big?

359
00:19:16,567 --> 00:19:18,200
Wow, this guy's ballsy!

360
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:20,267
What do you want?
What do you want, huh?

361
00:19:20,267 --> 00:19:21,433
[JAMES] You think you're tough?

362
00:19:21,433 --> 00:19:22,367
Do we look like small fish
to you?

363
00:19:22,367 --> 00:19:24,633
[BINOY] Ah! Don't you know
who we are?

364
00:19:24,633 --> 00:19:26,233
You want your blood
to trickle down?

365
00:19:26,233 --> 00:19:27,567
I'll put this in your head!

366
00:19:27,567 --> 00:19:30,267
- I'll put it inside!
- Let's leave, Bullet.

367
00:19:30,300 --> 00:19:32,167
They'll only destroy
our mission.

368
00:19:32,167 --> 00:19:33,067
- Let's go.
- Okay.

369
00:19:33,067 --> 00:19:35,367
- They're approaching!
- Here I go!

370
00:19:36,167 --> 00:19:37,767
I almost had you.
Good thing you walked away.

371
00:19:37,767 --> 00:19:40,100
You know, if they didn't leave,
and I couldn't hold back,

372
00:19:40,100 --> 00:19:42,433
- I'll do this to them!
- The other guy's useless!

373
00:19:42,433 --> 00:19:44,133
His body's so big,
he's on asteroids!

374
00:19:44,133 --> 00:19:45,467
- What's "asteroid"?
- The one gym people

375
00:19:45,467 --> 00:19:47,800
- inject in their arms.
- Oh, yeah!

376
00:19:47,800 --> 00:19:53,767
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

377
00:19:53,767 --> 00:19:55,633
Sam, positive.

378
00:19:55,633 --> 00:19:58,400
- Mr. Chan's inside.
- How can you be sure?

379
00:19:58,400 --> 00:20:00,667
We pretended to buy,
and asked for a discount.

380
00:20:00,667 --> 00:20:03,300
The staff said she had
to ask her boss about it.

381
00:20:03,333 --> 00:20:05,667
[BULLET] We didn't stay long.
She might get suspicious.

382
00:20:05,667 --> 00:20:08,467
Alright. Let's wait here.

383
00:20:10,300 --> 00:20:17,267
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

384
00:20:32,267 --> 00:20:35,833
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

385
00:20:35,867 --> 00:20:37,867
- Sir Victor!
- Mr. Wang, how are you?

386
00:20:37,867 --> 00:20:39,000
I'm great, I'm great.

387
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:40,667
- How are you?
- Business is doing good.

388
00:20:40,667 --> 00:20:42,233
- [VICTOR] Good, good. Great.
- [WANG] Yes, yes.

389
00:20:42,233 --> 00:20:43,667
- Good to see you.
- Thank you. See you, see you!

390
00:20:43,667 --> 00:20:50,633
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

391
00:20:53,733 --> 00:20:57,733
[MONEY RUSTLING]

392
00:20:57,733 --> 00:21:00,233
- [CHAN] Is that ready?
- [WOMAN] Yes, Mr. Chan.

393
00:21:00,233 --> 00:21:03,400
- 200 million pesos.
- Okay, good.

394
00:21:03,400 --> 00:21:07,333
[PHONE RINGING]

395
00:21:08,600 --> 00:21:10,567
- Hello?
- Victor!

396
00:21:10,567 --> 00:21:12,433
Your money is ready.

397
00:21:12,433 --> 00:21:15,733
I'm sorry, Mr. Chan,
but I will be late.

398
00:21:15,733 --> 00:21:17,700
I have a wedding to attend.

399
00:21:17,700 --> 00:21:19,667
But, after this,
I'll go to the bar.

400
00:21:19,667 --> 00:21:21,267
[CHAN] Okay, no problem!

401
00:21:21,267 --> 00:21:25,500
My place is very near bar.
Anytime, I can go.

402
00:21:25,500 --> 00:21:26,500
See you, then.

403
00:21:27,700 --> 00:21:29,200
[LINE DROPS]

404
00:21:29,200 --> 00:21:36,200
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

405
00:21:38,067 --> 00:21:41,033
- What can we even do here?
- We need a side job, right?

406
00:21:41,033 --> 00:21:42,633
We could dance or sing.

407
00:21:43,567 --> 00:21:44,233
We could even rap!

408
00:21:44,367 --> 00:21:45,567
Anything to earn money.

409
00:21:45,733 --> 00:21:47,067
You know the drill.

410
00:21:47,233 --> 00:21:49,500
Drop a coin, distract,
and steal.

411
00:21:49,600 --> 00:21:50,767
- Hey.
- Hey, you know,

412
00:21:50,933 --> 00:21:52,433
I'm going to tell
on you to Gabo.

413
00:21:52,600 --> 00:21:53,733
Hey, I was just kidding.

414
00:21:53,867 --> 00:21:56,067
- "Just kidding?"
- Let's find a spot to sing at.

415
00:21:56,233 --> 00:21:57,333
What about here?

416
00:21:57,433 --> 00:21:59,567
[GUITAR STRUMMING]

417
00:21:59,700 --> 00:22:01,200
Hey, Mister!

418
00:22:01,300 --> 00:22:02,733
May we borrow your guitar?

419
00:22:02,900 --> 00:22:05,067
I'll give you 50 pesos so
you can buy some food.

420
00:22:05,233 --> 00:22:08,500
Sure, there's not a lot of
generous people today.

421
00:22:08,600 --> 00:22:10,067
Well, that works for us.

422
00:22:10,233 --> 00:22:11,700
[IPE] Here's 50 pesos.

423
00:22:12,733 --> 00:22:14,167
You jerk!

424
00:22:14,267 --> 00:22:16,400
This is just 20 pesos.
You're tricking me!

425
00:22:16,567 --> 00:22:17,700
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

426
00:22:17,800 --> 00:22:20,133
Why, this jerk!
You're not blind!

427
00:22:20,300 --> 00:22:22,600
That's none of your business!
You do what earns you money!

428
00:22:22,767 --> 00:22:25,267
Just take care of my guitar.

429
00:22:25,433 --> 00:22:27,633
If you break this,
I'll be looking for you three.

430
00:22:27,800 --> 00:22:30,067
- Okay, fine!
- All right.

431
00:22:30,167 --> 00:22:31,867
Hand it over.

432
00:22:31,967 --> 00:22:33,367
I'll borrow this too, okay?

433
00:22:33,467 --> 00:22:34,767
Take care of that!

434
00:22:34,933 --> 00:22:36,767
We'd miss out if
we just stayed here.

435
00:22:36,900 --> 00:22:38,567
It's Chinese New Year.

436
00:22:38,667 --> 00:22:40,767
- We can earn a lot of money.
- Right!

437
00:22:40,900 --> 00:22:42,267
We could've taken a gig.

438
00:22:42,400 --> 00:22:44,367
So what are we waiting for?
Let's leave for now.

439
00:22:44,467 --> 00:22:47,033
There's a lot of people handing
out red envelopes in Chinatown.

440
00:22:47,133 --> 00:22:49,267
What if Gabo looks for us?
He'll punish us for sure.

441
00:22:49,433 --> 00:22:51,500
He won't look for us.
That's not going to happen.

442
00:22:51,667 --> 00:22:53,800
If he'll come here,
he'll call us first.

443
00:22:53,933 --> 00:22:54,967
[TOLITS] Right?

444
00:22:55,133 --> 00:22:56,833
Let's get going.
Let's not waste time.

445
00:22:58,100 --> 00:23:00,600
[BONG AND IPE] One, two,
three, four!

446
00:23:00,700 --> 00:23:03,467
[SINGING]<i> Every Filipino
</i> Sing with us

447
00:23:03,600 --> 00:23:05,900
<i> Happy Chinese New Year</i>

448
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:08,833
<i>Every Filipino-Chinese
Sing with us</i>

449
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:11,800
<i> Happy Chinese New Year</i>

450
00:23:11,933 --> 00:23:14,300
<i>Happy Chinese New Year
Have a prosperous new year</i>

451
00:23:14,433 --> 00:23:16,933
<i> What a timely celebration</i>

452
00:23:17,033 --> 00:23:19,267
<i>Make sure to use every
opportunity wisely</i>

453
00:23:19,367 --> 00:23:22,167
Especially because the sleeping
<i> dragons have awakened</i>

454
00:23:22,367 --> 00:23:24,000
[TRADITIONAL CHINESE
MUSIC PLAYING]

455
00:23:24,133 --> 00:23:26,800
<i> Dances and drums making noise</i>

456
00:23:26,900 --> 00:23:29,500
<i>Sticky rice cakes
They're giving away</i>

457
00:23:29,633 --> 00:23:32,467
[TRADITIONAL CHINESE
MUSIC CONTINUES]

458
00:23:32,567 --> 00:23:33,833
[TOLITS] Hey! Why are you there?

459
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:35,500
We shouldn't go there!

460
00:23:35,633 --> 00:23:37,767
You should go here
at the right side!

461
00:23:37,867 --> 00:23:40,267
You're just looking at
the girls there!

462
00:23:40,367 --> 00:23:42,700
Ouch! Ouch! Hey!

463
00:23:42,867 --> 00:23:44,700
[RAPPING]
<i> Happy Chinese New Year!</i>

464
00:23:44,867 --> 00:23:47,833
<i> Come on, everybody!</i>

465
00:23:47,967 --> 00:23:50,533
<i> Kung Hei Fat Choi!</i>

466
00:23:50,700 --> 00:23:52,500
Bro, these guys are good.

467
00:23:53,300 --> 00:23:55,600
Yeah. They sound
like real rappers.

468
00:23:55,733 --> 00:23:57,000
[BULLET CHUCKLES]

469
00:23:58,433 --> 00:24:00,500
Ignore them.

470
00:24:00,600 --> 00:24:01,700
Stay focused on the target.

471
00:24:01,833 --> 00:24:03,367
We can't let them slip away.

472
00:24:03,500 --> 00:24:04,533
Copy, Captain.

473
00:24:05,433 --> 00:24:07,533
[RAPPING]
<i> Sometimes life's so hard,</i>

474
00:24:07,700 --> 00:24:09,233
<i>you don't even know
how real change</i>

475
00:24:09,400 --> 00:24:10,500
<i> can ever happen.</i>

476
00:24:10,600 --> 00:24:12,667
[FARTS]

477
00:24:12,767 --> 00:24:14,033
Damn, that stinks!
Who farted?

478
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:15,667
Daboy, give us a warning
next time!

479
00:24:15,767 --> 00:24:16,700
That wasn't me!

480
00:24:16,867 --> 00:24:18,033
[RETCHES]

481
00:24:18,167 --> 00:24:19,533
The smell's sticking
to my clothes!

482
00:24:19,700 --> 00:24:21,067
- [TOLITS] Hey, wait!
- [RETCHES]

483
00:24:21,233 --> 00:24:22,367
[RETCHES]

484
00:24:22,500 --> 00:24:23,667
[WOMAN] Hey, what the hell?

485
00:24:24,433 --> 00:24:26,333
Don't stay there!
We're working here.

486
00:24:26,433 --> 00:24:27,533
Get inside!

487
00:24:28,900 --> 00:24:31,267
<i> Kung Hei Fat Choi!</i>

488
00:24:31,433 --> 00:24:33,767
[TEKLA SINGING]

489
00:24:36,033 --> 00:24:38,667
Limbaga, Borromeo, and I
are changing positions.

490
00:24:38,767 --> 00:24:40,433
All right. Be careful.

491
00:24:40,600 --> 00:24:43,033
We're on a mission,
and you're still flirting.

492
00:24:44,900 --> 00:24:46,067
Let's go.

493
00:24:46,900 --> 00:24:49,700
<i> Come on, everybody!</i>

494
00:24:49,800 --> 00:24:51,900
<i> Kung Hei Fat Choi!</i>

495
00:24:52,067 --> 00:24:54,900
<i> Come on, everybody!</i>

496
00:24:55,067 --> 00:24:57,400
<i> Kung Hei Fat Choi!</i>

497
00:24:57,533 --> 00:24:58,667
[TEKLA] Let's hear it!

498
00:24:58,767 --> 00:25:01,167
- Give us a round of applause!
- [APPLAUSE]

499
00:25:01,267 --> 00:25:03,100
- [BONG] We're exhausted!
- [TEKLA] Yeah.

500
00:25:03,300 --> 00:25:04,767
[IPE] That's it!

501
00:25:04,900 --> 00:25:06,400
[BONG] If anyone else
wants to chip in...

502
00:25:07,433 --> 00:25:08,567
<i> Kung Hei Fat Choi!</i>

503
00:25:08,667 --> 00:25:10,100
[CROWD CHEERING]

504
00:25:10,267 --> 00:25:11,800
[IPE] For those who haven't
donated yet!

505
00:25:11,967 --> 00:25:13,967
[CROWD CHEERING]

506
00:25:14,133 --> 00:25:15,800
We worked hard for this!

507
00:25:17,133 --> 00:25:18,700
Show us some love!

508
00:25:18,800 --> 00:25:20,067
- [GABO] Hey!
- [BONG] Gabo!

509
00:25:20,167 --> 00:25:21,267
Any news?

510
00:25:21,400 --> 00:25:22,800
Oh.

511
00:25:22,967 --> 00:25:24,133
Well?
Have you found him?

512
00:25:24,300 --> 00:25:25,367
Not yet.

513
00:25:25,467 --> 00:25:28,133
We even posed as rappers
so we wouldn't look suspicious.

514
00:25:28,300 --> 00:25:30,600
Maybe we'll spot someone
keeping watch around here.

515
00:25:30,733 --> 00:25:35,300
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

516
00:25:35,500 --> 00:25:42,300
- [CROWD CHEERING]
- [DRUMS AND CYMBALS PLAYING]

517
00:25:45,833 --> 00:25:52,000
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

518
00:25:52,167 --> 00:25:53,633
Are you sure
this will work, ma'am?

519
00:25:53,767 --> 00:25:56,233
Everything is at stake here.

520
00:25:56,333 --> 00:25:57,133
This will work.

521
00:25:57,300 --> 00:25:59,967
Mr. Chan will lead us
to Tiger.

522
00:26:00,100 --> 00:26:01,467
We just need to find them

523
00:26:01,600 --> 00:26:02,800
and catch them in the act.

524
00:26:02,933 --> 00:26:07,733
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

525
00:26:07,833 --> 00:26:09,767
[BONG] This was a nice gig,
Gabo.

526
00:26:09,900 --> 00:26:11,333
We made a lot of money.

527
00:26:11,467 --> 00:26:13,667
Let's not look for
Mr. Chan anymore.

528
00:26:13,800 --> 00:26:15,000
Maybe we can make
enough here

529
00:26:15,133 --> 00:26:16,700
to cover your father's
hospital bills.

530
00:26:16,867 --> 00:26:18,133
No.

531
00:26:19,000 --> 00:26:21,167
We need to catch Tiger.

532
00:26:22,300 --> 00:26:24,667
We're going to follow Mr. Chan

533
00:26:24,800 --> 00:26:28,667
because he'll lead us to Tiger.

534
00:26:28,833 --> 00:26:35,667
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

535
00:26:51,100 --> 00:26:58,167
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

536
00:27:01,900 --> 00:27:04,033
In times of need...

537
00:27:04,200 --> 00:27:08,900
<i>I don't believe
Gabo will help us!</i>

538
00:27:09,067 --> 00:27:10,967
<i> I will figure this out.</i>

539
00:27:11,067 --> 00:27:12,200
<i> What are you going to do?</i>

540
00:27:12,333 --> 00:27:14,333
<i>She's applying for a job.
Help her out.</i>

541
00:27:14,433 --> 00:27:17,000
<i>Have you forgotten
what your family has done to us?</i>

542
00:27:17,133 --> 00:27:19,400
<i>You've got some nerve
coming here asking for a favor.</i>

543
00:27:19,567 --> 00:27:20,900
<i> Rudy really needs our help.</i>

544
00:27:21,067 --> 00:27:22,667
<i>Alright. You need help
with his funeral?</i>

545
00:27:22,767 --> 00:27:23,900
<i> With his treatment!</i>

546
00:27:24,067 --> 00:27:28,367
<i>I hired Betchay so I could
use her against Gabo.</i>

547
00:27:28,467 --> 00:27:30,767
Courage is needed.

548
00:27:30,933 --> 00:27:33,033
<i>I'm going in to see
if Mr. Chan's there.</i>

549
00:27:33,133 --> 00:27:34,900
<i>Tekla, find out if
Mr. Chan's inside.</i>

550
00:27:35,033 --> 00:27:36,733
<i>- Oh, that's beautiful.
- Excuse me.</i>

551
00:27:36,867 --> 00:27:38,000
<i> That item's reserved already.</i>

552
00:27:38,100 --> 00:27:40,067
<i>Oh? I don't see
anyone's name on it.</i>

553
00:27:40,233 --> 00:27:42,733
<i>You may be tall,
but I can take you on!</i>

554
00:27:42,867 --> 00:27:45,600
<i>Mr. Chan!
They're causing trouble!</i>

555
00:27:45,767 --> 00:27:47,033
<i>I have a meeting
at Jade Imperial.</i>

556
00:27:47,133 --> 00:27:49,033
<i>I know that place!
It's a popular bar nearby!</i>

557
00:27:49,167 --> 00:27:50,567
<i> The target's on the move.</i>

558
00:27:50,667 --> 00:27:51,767
<i> Target in sight.</i>

559
00:27:51,933 --> 00:27:54,800
<i>We'll follow him.
Let's meet there! Move!</i>

560
00:27:54,967 --> 00:27:56,900
<i> We need to catch Tiger.</i>
